  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-17, on the 0.23.0 build:\n\n> unclear if this is a bug.. but when the toolaxis A/B changes.. the \"heights\" should follow with the rotation.. Otherwise the calculations will be hard to preview..\n\nWhat happens: an operation has a tool axis that is turned (A/B, a 3+2 orientation). The height planes of the operation (clearance, retract, feed, top, bottom) in the viewport stay at their position and direction for the unturned axis.\n\nExpected: the height planes are drawn at right angles to the tool axis of the operation. When A or B changes, the planes turn with the axis. The preview then shows the levels that the generation uses.\n\nTo find first (the worker comments the answer here):\n- If only the drawing is wrong, and the generation measures the heights along the turned tool axis. Then this is a display defect (`P3`).\n- If the generation measures the heights along the Z of the setup while the tool axis is turned. Then the toolpath is wrong: raise this issue to `P1` and say so.\n- Which operation kinds have a turned tool axis and a heights page.\n\nRelated: #763 (one machining-frame seam, `OpFrame` and `TiltedFrame`), #2382 (operations start from the world origin).\n\n`effort:high` by the safety floor: the correction can touch the frame that generation uses.\n\nDone means:\n- A test pins the normal and the position of each height plane for an operation with a turned tool axis.\n- A test pins that the generation and the preview use the same frame for the heights.\n- Before/after screenshots are in the PR body.\n",
